{"url": "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/academics/graduate-program/graduate-programs-in-materials-science-and-engineering/index.html", "final_url": "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/academics/graduate-program/graduate-programs-in-materials-science-and-engineering/", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-24", "text": "Graduate Programs in Materials Science and Engineering\n/College of Engineering and Applied Sciences\nSearch this site\n\u00d7\nSearch\nSearch\nMaterials Science and Chemical Engineering\nAbout\nChair\u2019s Message and Fast Facts\nAdministration and Staff\nExecutive Committee Members\nAcademics\nOverview\nUndergraduate Programs\nChemical and Molecular Engineering\nEngineering Science\nGraduate Programs\nChemical and Molecular Engineering\nMaterials Science and Engineering\nStudents\nOpportunities\nStudent Spotlights\nSeminar and Student Events\nStudent Resources\nForms\nFaculty\nOverview\nPostdocs and Research Scientists\nNS Adjunct Faculty\nFaculty Resources\nResearch\nResearch Areas\nCenters and Institutes\nConnect\nDirections\nMentor Connect\nAlumni Spotlight\nNews\nGiving\nWays to Give\nDonors\nMore\nHOME\nAbout\nChair\u2019s Message and Fast Facts\nAdministration and Staff\nExecutive Committee Members\nAcademics\nOverview\nUndergraduate Programs\nChemical and Molecular Engineering\nEngineering Science\nGraduate Programs\nChemical and Molecular Engineering\nMaterials Science and Engineering\nStudents\nOpportunities\nStudent Spotlights\nSeminar and Student Events\nStudent Resources\nForms\nFaculty\nOverview\nPostdocs and Research Scientists\nNS Adjunct Faculty\nFaculty Resources\nResearch\nResearch Areas\nCenters and Institutes\nConnect\nDirections\nMentor Connect\nAlumni Spotlight\nNews\nGiving\nWays to Give\nDonors\nMore\n\u00d7\nSearch\nSearch\nCollege of Engineering and Applied SciencesMaterials Science and Chemical Engineering\nHome\nAbout\nChair\u2019s Message and Fast Facts\nAdministration and Staff\nExecutive Committee Members\nAcademics\nOverview\nUndergraduate Programs\nChemical and Molecular Engineering\nEngineering Science\nGraduate Programs\nChemical and Molecular Engineering\nMaterials Science and Engineering\nStudents\nOpportunities\nStudent Spotlights\nSeminar and Student Events\nStudent Resources\nForms\nFaculty\nOverview\nPostdocs and Research Scientists\nNS Adjunct Faculty\nFaculty Resources\nResearch\nResearch Areas\nCenters and Institutes\nConnect\nDirections\nMentor Connect\nAlumni Spotlight\nNews\nGiving\nWays to Give\nDonors\nMaterials Science and Chemical Engineering\nAcademics\nGraduate Program\nGraduate Program in Materials Science and Engineering\nGraduate Program\nin Materials Science and Engineering\nWith a projected 7% growth in materials engineering jobs (2023\u20132033), Stony Brook\nUniversity\u2019s STEM-designated MS and PhD programs in Materials Science and Engineering\nprepare students for impactful careers across industry, research, academia, and government\nlaboratories. Through advanced, interdisciplinary training and close collaboration\nwith world-class faculty and research centers, students develop expertise in areas\nsuch as energy storage, nanotechnology, biomaterials, semiconductors, coatings, and\nsustainable materials. Graduates are equipped to lead innovation and technology development\nacross sectors including aerospace, electronics, energy, healthcare, and manufacturing.\nApply now\nRequest for information\nGraduate Program Committee\nGraduate Courses\nGraduate Advising\nApplication Deadlines\nMS in Materials Science and Engineering: Program Overview\nBuild a strong foundation in materials theory, advanced applications, and experimental\ntechniques through a flexible M.S. program designed for both industry careers and\nadvanced study. With options to tailor your experience, the program emphasizes hands-on\nresearch, analytical problem-solving, and real-world application, preparing you to\ninnovate across a wide range of materials-driven fields.\nMS Program Highlights\n30 credits \u2013 flexible full-time or part-time study\nThesis and non-thesis tracks aligned with your career goals\nStrong focus on hands-on research and experimental techniques\nDevelop critical skills in analysis, design, and materials innovation\nPrepares you for industry roles or continued PhD/professional study\nGraduate MS Catalog\nPhD in Materials Science and Engineering: Program Overview\nLead innovation at the forefront of materials research through a dynamic Ph.D. program\nthat combines advanced coursework with original, high-impact research. Explore cutting-edge\nareas such as nanotechnology, biomaterials, energy storage, coatings, and semiconductors,\nwhile working alongside expert faculty and collaborating with premier research centers\nlike Brookhaven National Laboratory and the Garcia Polymer Center. With a strong emphasis\non real-world problem-solving, interdisciplinary training, and professional development,\nthe program prepares graduates for leadership roles in academia, industry, and research\ninstitutions.\nPhD Program Highlights\n60 credits \u2013 full-time study combining coursework and research\nFully funded through research and teaching assistantships\nResearch opportunities in energy storage, nanotechnology, biomaterials, coatings,\nand semiconductors\nDevelop leadership and mentoring skills through teaching and research roles\nCulminates in comprehensive exams and a doctoral dissertation defense\nGraduate PhD Catalog\nLife After Graduation\nMS Career Paths\nMaterials Engineer\nProduct Development\nProcess Engineering\nR&D Engineer\nQuality Engineering\nPhD Career Paths\nAcademic and Faculty Careers\nSenior Scientist Roles\nNational Laboratory Research\nMaterials Innovation Leadership\nKey Industries\nAerospace and Defense\nBiomedical Technology\nElectronics and Semiconductors\nEnergy and Sustainability\nAdvanced Materials\nRecent Employers\nApplied Materials, Intel, Google, Pratt & Whitney, Sandia National Laboratories, and\nmore.\nBack to Graduate Program\nMaterials Science and Chemical Engineering\n314 Engineering Building | Stony Brook University\nPHONE: 631-632-4986 | EMAIL: msce_office@stonybrook.edu\nPrivacy Policy\nReporting Discrimination\nSexual Misconduct\nAccessibility Barrier\n\u00a9 2026 Stony Brook University\n\u00a9", "links": [["", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/"], ["College of Engineering and Applied Sciences", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ceas/"], ["Materials Science and Chemical Engineering", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng//index.html"], ["", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/index.html"], ["About", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/about/index.html"], ["Chair\u2019s Message and Fast Facts", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/about/chairs_message_and_fast_facts.html"], ["Administration and Staff", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/about/administration_and_staff.html"], ["Executive Committee Members", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/about/executive-committee-members.html"], ["Academics", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/academics/index.html"], ["Overview", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/academics/overview.html"], ["Undergraduate Programs", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/academics/undergraduate-programs/index.html"], ["Chemical and Molecular Engineering", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/academics/undergraduate-programs/undergraduate-program-in-chemical-and-molecular-engineering/index.html"], ["Engineering Science", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/academics/undergraduate-programs/undergraduate-program-in-engineering-science/index.html"], ["Graduate Programs", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/academics/graduate-program/index.html"], ["Chemical and Molecular Engineering", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/academics/graduate-program/graduate-programs-in-chemical-and-molecular-engineering/index.html"], ["Materials